+        // their textures, so each rect asks for its slide (askSlide()), and it is written once they all have, only to an
+        // entry every call drawn from it asked the same of: a call that asks nothing, still or unpaired, asks for no
+        // slide. Mario Golf's lens flare draws its eight circles from one texture, and as the one beyond the sun was cut
+        // a few rows further at the screen's corner each frame, its texture's slide moved the other seven's too: between
+        // the game's frames each showed the rim of its mirrored texture as a cap over it.
+        struct TileSlide {
